# The eighth tooling step, part `stalls`: `cargo xtask ci` runs a cluster of
# timeouts again once when the disk stalled, and does not judge a stalled
# run's tiers at a desk (docs/testing-and-ci.md, "Running the tests many
# times over" and "Budgets are enforced").

# The tier check: judged on CI whatever the pressure, not judged at a desk
# over the threshold.

[break] a-stalled-run-is-not-judged-on-ci-either
rule: On CI the tiers are judged whatever the pressure: a verdict that moved with a reading nobody can check there would be a loophole.
file: xtask/src/stall.rs
in: judge
find: if in_actions {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    stall::tests::a_run_that_stalled_for_a_tenth_of_its_time_is_not_judged_away_from_ci

[break] a-run-at-the-threshold-is-judged
rule: A run that stalled for a tenth of its time or more is not judged: the threshold is inclusive.
file: xtask/src/stall.rs
in: judge
find: share >= STALLED_SHARE
replace: share > STALLED_SHARE
caught-by:
    stall::tests::a_run_that_stalled_for_a_tenth_of_its_time_is_not_judged_away_from_ci

[break] only-the-first-test-run-is-counted-for-the-tiers
rule: The tier check reads both test runs, and a re-run: their stall times and their times are added.
file: xtask/src/stall.rs
in: judge
find: records.iter().map(|record| record.full_us).sum()
replace: records.first().map_or(0, |record| record.full_us)
caught-by:
    stall::tests::a_run_that_stalled_for_a_tenth_of_its_time_is_not_judged_away_from_ci

[break] the-threshold-is-half-the-run
rule: A run is taken to have stalled when every task waited on I/O for a tenth of its time, as mutate's busy disk is.
file: xtask/src/stall.rs
find: pub(crate) const STALLED_SHARE: f64 = 10.0;
replace: pub(crate) const STALLED_SHARE: f64 = 50.0;
caught-by:
    stall::tests::a_run_that_stalled_for_a_tenth_of_its_time_is_not_judged_away_from_ci
    stall::rerun::tests::the_threshold_is_a_tenth_of_the_runs_time_and_not_a_hair_under

[break] the-share-is-not-a-percentage
rule: The share of a run that the disk stalled is a percentage of the run's own time.
file: xtask/src/stall.rs
in: percent
find: 100.0 * stalled / run
replace: stalled / run
caught-by:
    stall::tests::a_runs_stall_is_the_share_of_its_own_time_every_task_waited
    stall::tests::a_run_that_stalled_for_a_tenth_of_its_time_is_not_judged_away_from_ci

[break] the-stall-is-the-pressure-since-boot
rule: A run's stall is the kernel's counter after the run less its value when the run started, not since boot.
file: xtask/src/stall.rs
in: stalled_seconds
find: self.after.full_total.saturating_sub(self.before.full_total)
replace: self.after.full_total
caught-by:
    stall::tests::a_runs_stall_is_the_share_of_its_own_time_every_task_waited

[break] the-record-is-the-pressure-since-boot
rule: What the tier check is told of a run is the stall time of that run, not since boot.
file: xtask/src/stall.rs
in: record
find: full_us: self.after.full_total.saturating_sub(self.before.full_total)
replace: full_us: self.after.full_total
caught-by:
    stall::tests::a_runs_stall_is_the_share_of_its_own_time_every_task_waited

[break] the-pressure-file-variable-is-ignored
rule: A file named in CORTEX_PRESSURE_FILE is read in place of the kernel's, so that tests give the decisions a recorded pressure.
file: xtask/src/stall.rs
in: read_pressure_with
find: Some(file) => read_pressure_from(Path::new(&file)),
replace: Some(_) => read_kernel_pressure(),
caught-by:
    stall::tests::a_pressure_can_be_read_from_the_file_a_variable_names

# The re-run's decision.

[break] a-cluster-at-the-threshold-is-not-run-again
rule: A cluster of timeouts is run again when the disk stalled for a tenth of the run or more.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: decide
find: observed.share() < STALLED_SHARE
replace: observed.share() <= STALLED_SHARE
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::the_threshold_is_a_tenth_of_the_runs_time_and_not_a_hair_under

[break] a-cluster-is-run-again-whatever-the-pressure
rule: A cluster of timeouts on a disk that did not stall is a failure, and is not run again.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: decide
find: observed.share() < STALLED_SHARE
replace: false
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::a_cluster_without_a_stall_is_not_run_again
    stall::rerun::tests::a_cluster_on_a_quiet_disk_runs_once_and_fails

[break] a-name-a-filter-cannot-hold-is-run-again
rule: A test whose name a filter cannot be trusted to match exactly is not run again.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: decide
find: !nameable(&test.binary) || !nameable(&test.name)
replace: false
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::a_test_whose_name_a_filter_cannot_name_exactly_is_not_run_again

[break] a-bracket-is-a-nameable-character
rule: A test whose name has a `)` in it is not run again: a filter's matcher ends at one.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: nameable
find: '_' | ':' | '/' | '.' | '-'
replace: '_' | ':' | '/' | '.' | '-' | ')'
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::a_test_whose_name_a_filter_cannot_name_exactly_is_not_run_again

[break] the-filter-chooses-tests-that-match-either-half
rule: A test is run again by its binary and its name together, not by one of them.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: filter
find: "(binary_id(={}) and test(={}))"
replace: "(binary_id(={}) or test(={}))"
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::the_filter_names_each_test_by_its_binary_and_name_exactly

[break] the-filter-matches-a-name-by-part
rule: A test is chosen by its exact name: a name that is the end of another's is another test.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: filter
find: "(binary_id(={}) and test(={}))"
replace: "(binary_id(={}) and test(~{}))"
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::the_filter_names_each_test_by_its_binary_and_name_exactly

[break] the-reruns-filter-is-after-the-tests-arguments
rule: The filter of a re-run comes before any argument for the test binaries, which `--` begins.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: with_filter
find: .position(|argument| argument == "--")
replace: .position(|argument| argument == "-- ")
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::the_filter_takes_the_place_of_the_runs_own_and_comes_before_the_tests_arguments

[break] the-reruns-filter-is-given-beside-the-runs-own
rule: A re-run runs the cluster's tests and no others: the run's own filter is taken out, as nextest runs a test that matches any filterset.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: with_filter
find: let (_, mut rest) = crate::checks::filtersets(run);
replace: let mut rest = run.to_vec();
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::the_filter_takes_the_place_of_the_runs_own_and_comes_before_the_tests_arguments

[break] a-test-that-passed-on-its-retry-is-a-failure-to-run-again
rule: Only a test that failed is run again: one that passed on its retry did not fail.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: run
find: junit::failed(&first_report)
replace: junit::failures(&first_report)
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::tests_that_passed_on_their_retry_are_no_cluster_to_run_again

# What the re-run leaves, and when the step passes.

[break] a-timeout-that-recurs-is-a-pass
rule: A test that times out again on the re-run fails the step.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: rerun
find: if not_passed > 0 {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::a_timeout_that_recurs_on_the_rerun_fails_the_step
    stall::rerun::tests::a_test_that_is_not_in_the_reruns_report_fails_the_step

[break] another-failure-beside-the-rerun-is-forgiven
rule: A failure of another kind, and a timeout outside the cluster, still fail the step: a re-run that passes hides nothing else.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: rerun
find: others.len().saturating_sub(not_passed)
replace: 0
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::a_failure_of_another_kind_beside_a_rerun_that_passes_still_fails_the_step

[break] a-rerun-whose-command-failed-passes
rule: A re-run whose own command failed fails the step, whatever its report says.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: rerun
find: problems.push(format!("the re-run's own command failed: {error}"));
replace: let _ = error;
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::a_rerun_whose_command_failed_fails_the_step_whatever_its_report_says

[break] the-step-passes-with-problems
rule: The step passes only when nothing is left that failed.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: rerun
find: if problems.is_empty() {
replace: if true {
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::a_timeout_that_recurs_on_the_rerun_fails_the_step
    stall::rerun::tests::a_failure_of_another_kind_beside_a_rerun_that_passes_still_fails_the_step

[break] a-test-missing-from-the-rerun-passed
rule: A test that is not in the re-run's report went missing, and fails the step.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: verdicts
find: None => Verdict::Missing,
replace: None => Verdict::Passed,
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::a_test_that_is_not_in_the_reruns_report_fails_the_step
    stall::rerun::tests::each_test_that_was_run_again_is_judged_by_the_reruns_own_report

[break] a-timeout-on-the-rerun-is-another-failure
rule: A test that times out again is said to have timed out again, not to have failed.
file: xtask/src/stall/rerun.rs
in: verdicts
find: failure.kind.contains("timeout")
replace: !failure.kind.contains("timeout")
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::each_test_that_was_run_again_is_judged_by_the_reruns_own_report

# The report.

[break] replacements-are-made-from-the-start
rule: The cases of the tests run again are replaced from the end of the report, so that a longer case does not move the ones after it.
file: xtask/src/junit.rs
in: replace_cases
find: spans(first).iter().rev()
replace: spans(first).iter()
caught-by:
    stall::rerun::tests::a_rerun_that_passes_replaces_the_timeouts_and_the_step_passes

[break] a-case-is-replaced-by-one-of-another-name
rule: A test's case is replaced by the case of the same binary and name from the re-run, and by no other.
file: xtask/src/junit.rs
in: replace_cases
find: .find(|new| new.binary == ours.binary && new.name == ours.name)
replace: .find(|new| new.binary == ours.binary)
caught-by:
    junit::tests::cases_put_in_the_place_of_others_leave_the_rest_and_the_counts_true

[break] the-reports-failure-count-is-not-made-again
rule: A report does not say a failure that is no longer in it: its failures are counted again from its cases.
file: xtask/src/junit.rs
in: recount
find: let open = with_attribute(open, "failures", &failures_total.to_string());
replace: let open = open.to_owned();
caught-by:
    junit::tests::cases_put_in_the_place_of_others_leave_the_rest_and_the_counts_true
    stall::rerun::tests::a_rerun_that_passes_replaces_the_timeouts_and_the_step_passes

[break] a-suites-failure-count-is-not-made-again
rule: Each suite's failures are counted again from its cases too.
file: xtask/src/junit.rs
in: recount
find: let new_tag = with_attribute(tag, "failures", &failures.to_string());
replace: let new_tag = tag.to_owned();
caught-by:
    junit::tests::cases_put_in_the_place_of_others_leave_the_rest_and_the_counts_true

# The wiring of the tier check.

[break] the-tier-check-judges-on-ci-as-at-a-desk
rule: The tier check is told where it runs, and judges CI whatever the pressure.
file: xtask/src/tiers.rs
in: check_ci_report_in
find: stall::judge(in_actions, &records)
replace: stall::judge(false, &records)
caught-by:
    tiers::tests::a_stalled_run_is_not_judged_at_a_desk_and_is_on_ci_whatever_the_pressure

[break] the-tier-check-never-hears-of-a-stall
rule: A run that stalled is not judged at a desk.
file: xtask/src/tiers.rs
in: check_ci_report_in
find: stall::judge(in_actions, &records)
replace: None,
caught-by:
    tiers::tests::a_stalled_run_is_not_judged_at_a_desk_and_is_on_ci_whatever_the_pressure

[break] a-run-not-judged-goes-on-to-fail-a-tier
rule: A run that is not judged neither passes nor fails a budget.
file: xtask/src/tiers.rs
in: check_report_with
find: if stalled.is_some() {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    tiers::tests::a_stalled_run_is_not_judged_at_a_desk_and_is_on_ci_whatever_the_pressure

[break] a-run-not-judged-marks-its-tiers
rule: A run that is not judged has no mark on a tier, over budget or far over it.
file: xtask/src/tiers.rs
in: summarise_marked
find: verdict(above_start, budget).filter(|_| marked)
replace: verdict(above_start, budget)
caught-by:
    tiers::tests::a_run_that_is_not_judged_has_no_mark_on_any_tier

[break] the-build-keeps-the-last-runs-pressure
rule: The build forgets what the pressure said of an earlier run, so that a stale record does not keep the next run's tiers from being judged.
file: xtask/src/checks.rs
in: forget_reports
find: workspace::forget_report(&crate::stall::record_path(root))
replace: Ok(())
caught-by:
    checks::tests::what_the_pressure_said_of_an_earlier_run_is_forgotten_with_its_reports
